Okay, I've made an update to the patch, in which the following has been
added:

* Spell resistance no longer stops force bolts and Death's random
one-hit-kill.
* As requested, Turn to Stone replaces the Touch of Death monster
spell. When cast, it starts the "slow" petrification process.
* New spells providing temporary full resistances: "ward against fire"
(level 3), "ward against cold" (level 3), "ward against shocks" (level
3), "ward against spells" (level 5), and "reflection" (level 5). They
function for about the same amount of turns that "haste self" functions
for.
* These spells, as well as the "protection" spell, are now grouped
under the "protection spells" skill. Priests and wizards can reach
expert, healers and knights can reach skilled, and monks and samurai
can reach basic.
* It is worth advancing to expert skill.
* Spellbooks of ward against fire can't be burned.
* Spellbooks of ward against spells can't be cursed by malignant auras.

In case you forgot, the link is http://www.greyfire.org/~l/resist.diff



